<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95115" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπ-ιά</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπ-ιή</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lookout-place</i>,
			in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> esp. a <i>hill-top</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπιὴν εἰς παιπαλόεσσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					10.97
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ σκοπιῆς εἶδεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.275
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.524
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥμενος ἐν σκοπιῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.771
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπτῆρας δὲ κατὰ σκοπιὰς ὤτρυνα
				νέεσθαι</span> each to his <i>lookout-place</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.261
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγγελος . . ἀπὸ τηλαυγέος
				φαινόμενος ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				550
			</span></i>; <i>watch-tower</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥσπερ ἀπὸ ς. μοι φαίνεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					445c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>peak, height</i>, of Cithaeron, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				130
			</span></i>; of Athos, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				237
			</span></i> (anap.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰλιὰς ς</span>., of the
			Trojan acropolis, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				931
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ph.</u>
				233
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				281
			</span></i> (lyr.), etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θάσου σκοπιαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>JHS</u>
					29.93
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				9.47
			</span></i>:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπιαί</span>
			personified as women (<span class="entity">Oreads</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				2.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>look-out, watch</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπιὴν
			ἔχειν</span> to keep <i>watch</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.302
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔ κῃ πρόσω ς. ἔχοντες τούτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.13
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρυπταὶ ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Eq.Mag.</u>
				4.10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπιὴν φυλάσσειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arat.
					883
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
